# Base URL of the backend API. Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed
# to the client (Vite convention).
#
# Leave empty (or unset) to use same-origin relative paths. In dev, requests to
# /api are proxied to the backend by vite.config.ts. Set this to a full origin
# to call a cross-origin API directly, e.g. in production:
#
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
#
# The base is also the auth origin when web login is on: /auth/login,
# /auth/logout and /auth/me live on it, and the session cookie is host-scoped to
# it. In auth-on dev browse http://127.0.0.1:5173 with
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001 — both sides must be 127.0.0.1 (never
# mix in localhost), because the cookie is stored under 127.0.0.1.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
